Dialogue: 0,0:01:33.78,0:01:36.99,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Domain Expansion: Deadly Sentencing.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:38.29,0:01:39.00,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}A domain?!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:39.95,0:01:43.25,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'll take him down before he can activate it!
Dialogue: 0,0:01:53.63,0:01:57.85,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,All acts of violence are prohibited in this space.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:58.18,0:01:59.56,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,For both of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:01:59.56,0:02:00.60,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,For {\i1}both{\i0}?
Dialogue: 0,0:02:04.77,0:02:06.65,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Oh, sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:06.65,0:02:08.36,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Harmful remarks are the exception.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:09.28,0:02:11.90,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Judgeman, please begin.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:15.37,0:02:17.70,Default,Judgeman,0,0,0,,Itadori Yuji
Dialogue: 0,0:02:17.70,0:02:28.13,Default,Judgeman,0,0,0,,stands accused of entering the Maji Vegas gambling parlor \Nin Sendai City, Miyagi Prefecture, on July 16th, 2017,
Dialogue: 0,0:02:28.13,0:02:31.13,Default,Judgeman,0,0,0,,despite being under 18 at the time.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:31.63,0:02:32.51,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Huh?!
Dialogue: 0,0:02:33.51,0:02:34.22,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Oh.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:35.05,0:02:38.72,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Uh, well, um...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:38.72,0:02:42.52,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Judgeman knows everything about \Nthose within this domain.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:43.52,0:02:45.48,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,But don't worry.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:45.48,0:02:48.61,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,That information isn't shared with me.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:48.61,0:02:52.78,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,The verdict will be decided \Nsolely by the arguments we present.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:53.95,0:02:56.36,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,With the sole exception of this evidence.
Dialogue: 0,0:02:56.74,0:02:59.58,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Huh?! When did you...
Dialogue: 0,0:02:59.95,0:03:03.58,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,This is the evidence provided by Judgeman for this case.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:04.00,0:03:08.08,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,There is no guarantee \Nthat this will confirm the charges.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:08.67,0:03:11.34,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I also don't plan on telling you what it is.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:11.67,0:03:15.84,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Knowing that, you must now \Npresent your argument to clear suspicion
Dialogue: 0,0:03:15.84,0:03:18.97,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,and win a not guilty verdict from Judgeman.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:20.60,0:03:22.77,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}A court trial technique?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:24.73,0:03:27.90,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}That badge! So he really is a lawyer?
Dialogue: 0,0:03:28.31,0:03:30.82,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}But he's acting more like a prosecutor.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:32.07,0:03:36.70,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\fad(0,300)\i1}Higuruma is a modern sorcerer, \Nbut this domain is like what {*}Master Tengen{*Tengen-sama} mentioned.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:37.99,0:03:44.91,Default,Tengen,0,0,164,,Domains used to be a much more standard skill \Nfor sorcerers in the past.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:45.25,0:03:53.63,Default,Tengen,0,0,164,,That's because they lacked the "guaranteed kill" element of most modern domains' deadly guaranteed hit attacks.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:54.17,0:03:59.43,Default,Tengen,0,0,164,,They simply guaranteed that users' techniques \Nwould hit the target in the domain.
Dialogue: 0,0:03:59.89,0:04:03.68,Default,Tengen,0,0,164,,That was the common function \Nof domains in the past.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:04.35,0:04:06.68,Default,Tengen,0,0,164,,By focusing too hard \Non the "guaranteed kill" aspect,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:06.68,0:04:10.06,Default,Tengen,0,0,164,,sorcerers raised the bar on the \Nrequirements for constructing a domain,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:10.06,0:04:16.07,Default,Tengen,0,0,164,,{\fad(0,2000)}making it a more advanced skill \Nwith fewer practitioners.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:16.78,0:04:20.24,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}That means this domain is founded on Binding Vows
Dialogue: 0,0:04:20.24,0:04:28.21,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}preventing lethality, prohibiting physical harm, and requiring some explanation of its rules!
Dialogue: 0,0:04:30.04,0:04:32.50,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,You get one chance to make a statement.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:32.50,0:04:34.30,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,This also applies to both of us.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:34.75,0:04:39.80,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,After your statement, I get one chance \Nto make my rebuttal using this evidence,
Dialogue: 0,0:04:39.80,0:04:45.10,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,and then Judgeman announces his verdict \Nin accordance with the Six Codes.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:45.85,0:04:47.68,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,What happens if I'm judged guilty?
Dialogue: 0,0:04:48.31,0:04:52.31,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Unfortunately, I have no obligation \Nto answer that question.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:52.31,0:04:56.11,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Instead, I'll at least tell you this.
Dialogue: 0,0:04:57.11,0:04:59.15,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,You have three options:
Dialogue: 0,0:04:59.61,0:05:00.49,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Silence.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:00.49,0:05:01.36,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Confession.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:01.36,0:05:02.87,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Denial.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:02.87,0:05:05.91,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Your denial may include false statements.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:06.91,0:05:08.50,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,You mean I can just lie?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:09.00,0:05:10.37,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,In court?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:11.00,0:05:16.13,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,If everyone told the truth, \Nthere would be no need for trials.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:16.88,0:05:19.72,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Now, make your argument.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:19.72,0:05:22.01,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Judgeman is not very patient.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:24.43,0:05:30.27,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I did go to that gambling place. \NI played a few rounds. I might've even won.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:30.73,0:05:34.44,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I can't avoid lying if I want to claim innocence.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:34.44,0:05:37.40,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}What I actually need to consider is...
Dialogue: 0,0:05:37.78,0:05:39.49,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}what could be in that evidence!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:40.65,0:05:44.99,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,There is no guarantee \Nthat this will confirm the charges.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:46.37,0:05:47.16,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}One:
Dialogue: 0,0:05:47.16,0:05:50.71,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}if that evidence doesn't prove I entered the gambling parlor,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:50.71,0:05:52.50,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I just need to deny it or remain silent.
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.04,0:05:53.83,Default,Yuji,0,0,164,,{\an8}No!
Dialogue: 0,0:05:53.83,0:05:54.38,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Two:
Dialogue: 0,0:05:54.38,0:05:57.04,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}if the evidence only proves I entered it,
Dialogue: 0,0:05:57.04,0:05:59.84,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}should I gamble on an excuse that would earn leniency?
Dialogue: 0,0:05:59.17,0:06:01.59,Default,Yuji,0,0,164,,{\an8}I just went to the bathroom.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.59,0:06:03.47,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}But if the evidence is a bust,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:01.59,0:06:03.47,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,{\an8}So you did enter it, then!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.47,0:06:07.60,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I might be digging my own grave by admitting I entered it...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:03.47,0:06:05.14,Default,Yuji,0,0,164,,{\an8}Y-Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:07.89,0:06:09.06,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Three:
Dialogue: 0,0:06:09.06,0:06:13.31,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}if the evidence proves I not only entered it, but played the games,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:13.31,0:06:15.02,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm basically screwed.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:15.35,0:06:16.31,Default,Yuji,0,0,164,,{\an8}I'm sorry...
Dialogue: 0,0:06:16.31,0:06:19.36,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Should I bet on confessing to lighten my crime?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:19.36,0:06:22.53,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Does this court even offer lighter or heavier punishments?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:23.99,0:06:28.87,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,I did enter the Maji Vegas gambling parlor,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:29.41,0:06:33.04,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,but only because I suddenly needed to poop \Nand had no choice but to borrow their bathroom!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:34.37,0:06:35.54,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Is that so?
Dialogue: 0,0:06:35.92,0:06:37.63,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'm ditching option 3!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:37.63,0:06:41.17,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I don't know if this court \Naccepts extenuating circumstances,
Dialogue: 0,0:06:41.17,0:06:43.55,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}but this will leave the best impression!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:43.55,0:06:45.18,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I think!
Dialogue: 0,0:06:45.18,0:06:48.18,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,My turn, then.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:51.93,0:06:56.06,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,This is from the antique shop near Maji Vegas on the day in question.
Dialogue: 0,0:06:57.31,0:07:01.82,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,In essence, it's footage from \Nthe security camera of a cash exchange.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:05.40,0:07:10.83,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Would you agree the appearance and build all match Itadori Yuji here?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:14.75,0:07:17.04,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Since he just admitted to entering the parlor,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:17.04,0:07:22.51,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,this photo makes it clear his bathroom excuse \Nthe isn't worth believing.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:23.01,0:07:28.72,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,One can determine that despite being underage, \NItadori entered the parlor with the intent to play the games.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:30.10,0:07:33.47,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,What crime... would that be?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:34.02,0:07:38.81,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,The parlor explicitly prohibits minors from entering,
Dialogue: 0,0:07:39.27,0:07:41.48,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,so criminal trespassing. {illegal?}
Dialogue: 0,0:07:42.36,0:07:44.03,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Penal Code, Article 130.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:44.49,0:07:48.32,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,The Businesses Affecting Public Morals Regulation Act doesn't punish minors, after all.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:49.78,0:07:51.83,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,That wasn't fair.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:51.83,0:07:54.37,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,There was no way to talk my way out of it.
Dialogue: 0,0:07:54.37,0:07:56.12,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Should I have gone with option 3?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:56.12,0:07:58.04,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,What are you talking about?
Dialogue: 0,0:07:58.04,0:08:03.13,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Japan prohibits gambling, so parlors \Nand cash exchanges are separate legal entities.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:03.55,0:08:06.42,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Sometimes multiple parlors even share one.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:06.42,0:08:11.05,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,You were only on trial for entry into Maji Vegas.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:11.51,0:08:18.14,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,You simply needed to say, "I don't recognize \Nthat parlor," and deny the charge.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:19.06,0:08:21.40,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Wait, we haven't heard the verdict yet.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:27.95,0:08:29.20,Default,Judgeman,0,0,0,,{\an8}Guilty.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:29.20,0:08:30.70,Default,Judgeman,0,0,0,,{\an8}Confiscation.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:33.78,0:08:36.20,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}We're back where we were?
Dialogue: 0,0:08:36.20,0:08:39.71,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I was declared guilty, but I don't feel any different.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.71,0:08:39.83,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I was declared guilty, but I don't feel any different.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.83,0:08:39.96,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\pos(1142,1040)}I was declared guilty, but I don't feel any different.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:39.96,0:08:40.04,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\pos(1379,1080)}I was declared guilty, but I don't feel any different.
Dialogue: 0,0:08:48.92,0:08:50.09,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}That's...  {what the--}
Dialogue: 0,0:08:54.81,0:09:00.94,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Not only can he make that gavel \Nappear and disappear at will, he can alter its size too?!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:01.35,0:09:02.94,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}No, more importantly... {there's a bigger problem...}
Dialogue: 0,0:09:04.06,0:09:05.52,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,You're tough.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:06.19,0:09:08.49,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,That's the one thing I've got going for me.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:12.66,0:09:14.58,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}I can't control cursed energy!
Dialogue: 0,0:09:22.42,0:09:25.09,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Law apprenticeship period 59.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:25.09,0:09:30.72,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Iwate Bar Association's Hiromi Higuruma, age 36.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:31.72,0:09:34.01,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,He straightforwardly cleared all obstacles,
Dialogue: 0,0:09:34.01,0:09:37.56,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,like the entry exam to Tokyo University's School of Law
Dialogue: 0,0:09:37.56,0:09:40.48,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,and the old bar exam that preceded \Nthe institution of the law school system.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:41.48,0:09:50.24,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,To Higuruma, that was all a simple task of inputting and outputting the necessary knowledge.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:51.24,0:09:56.66,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,His peers whispered that he was a genius.
Dialogue: 0,0:09:56.66,0:10:04.17,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Yet the gem that shone brightest was his talent as a sorcerer.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:06.50,0:10:10.01,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,His technique came with his domain by default,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:10.01,0:10:14.51,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,but through analyzing that, \Nhe also learned the fundamentals of barriers.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:16.30,0:10:18.93,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Then, working backwards from barriers,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:18.93,0:10:22.31,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,he intuitively grasped manipulating cursed energy for physical enhancement. {cursed energy reinforcement}
Dialogue: 0,0:10:22.31,0:10:29.40,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Within twelve days of awakening, \Nhe had grown to match first-grade sorcerers.
Dialogue: 0,0:10:30.15,0:10:34.45,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Before entering the colony, \Nhe exorcised many cursed spirits,
Dialogue: 0,0:10:34.45,0:10:40.04,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,and struck down over \Ntwenty players who attacked him.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:17.24,0:11:19.91,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,You lost the ability to control cursed energy?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:21.08,0:11:22.70,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Didn't you do this?!
Dialogue: 0,0:11:24.20,0:11:29.34,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,The penalty of Confiscation makes it impossible to use one's cursed technique for some time.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:29.79,0:11:33.42,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I'm guessing you didn't have a cursed technique?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:34.17,0:11:38.93,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,That must be why the penalty \Nswitched to blocking the use of cursed energy.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:39.64,0:11:44.93,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Coincidentally, Confiscation is generally a supplementary sentence that's never imposed on its own.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:45.89,0:11:48.69,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's terrifying to think about.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:49.44,0:11:53.15,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}How can he hold his own against me \Nwithout cursed energy?
Dialogue: 0,0:11:53.82,0:11:57.40,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}He's using his natural physical prowess, \Nnot his might as a sorcerer.
Dialogue: 0,0:11:57.40,0:12:00.37,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}He must have frighteningly high physical durability.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:01.16,0:12:07.37,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}Sorcerers often struggle with basic cursed energy control \Nwhen they lose the use of their technique.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:07.92,0:12:10.50,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}Their instincts probably dull over the long years.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:10.50,0:12:14.38,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}But the complete inability to use cursed energy \Nis even more disadvantageous!
Dialogue: 0,0:12:14.84,0:12:17.72,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}Yet it's true that he can fight \Nthis well under these circumstances.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:18.38,0:12:22.60,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}My first strike would have \Nsettled the battle against most foes.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:23.60,0:12:25.81,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}If I'm not careful, he'll trip me up.
Dialogue: 0,0:12:26.98,0:12:28.52,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}I'll crush him with my full might!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:09.69,0:13:10.69,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,You're incredible!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:11.44,0:13:14.40,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}It's like I'm fighting an unbreakable doll.
Dialogue: 0,0:13:14.98,0:13:16.94,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Shit, shit, shit, shit, shit!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:16.94,0:13:18.44,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}How long will this last?!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:18.44,0:13:21.16,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}My cursed energy! \NHurry back to me, cursed energy!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:21.66,0:13:23.12,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}This is such a strong ability!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:23.12,0:13:27.16,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}There must be something! \NSomething that's a disadvantage for Higuruma!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:28.70,0:13:29.91,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Think!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:29.91,0:13:31.12,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Think, think!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:32.12,0:13:34.13,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}A technique for court trials...
Dialogue: 0,0:13:34.13,0:13:35.25,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,{\i1}Trials!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:43.01,0:13:44.26,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Higuruma!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:44.26,0:13:46.72,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,I want a retrial! One more time!
Dialogue: 0,0:13:56.52,0:13:58.03,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,You figured it out?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:00.44,0:14:01.95,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,That was close.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:01.95,0:14:04.49,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,I-I get a second trial, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:14:05.57,0:14:13.12,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,As long as the one judged guilty and penalized \Nby Judgeman doesn't admit their guilt,
Dialogue: 0,0:14:13.12,0:14:17.34,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,they can demand up to two retrials.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:17.84,0:14:21.55,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Judgeman cannot refuse them.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:23.88,0:14:26.01,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,All right, one more time!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:29.10,0:14:31.27,Default,Judgeman,0,0,0,,Itadori Yuji
Dialogue: 0,0:14:31.27,0:14:38.94,Default,Judgeman,0,0,0,,stands accused of mass murder in Shibuya \Non October 31st, 2018.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:42.03,0:14:44.11,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Yeah, I killed them.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:44.66,0:14:46.41,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,It's true. I won't deny it.
Dialogue: 0,0:14:49.24,0:14:50.79,Default,Judgeman,0,0,0,,{\an8}Guilty!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:50.79,0:14:52.79,Default,Judgeman,0,0,0,,{\an8}Confiscation!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:52.79,0:14:56.50,Default,Judgeman,0,0,0,,{\an8}Death Penalty!
Dialogue: 0,0:14:59.25,0:15:00.55,Default,Yoshizawa,0,0,0,,Higuruma{**-kun}.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:06.76,0:15:08.05,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,Yoshizawa{**-san}.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:09.30,0:15:12.02,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,I've already submitted the proposal.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:13.73,0:15:15.94,Default,Yoshizawa,0,0,164,,Oh, it's not about that.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:15.94,0:15:18.86,Default,Yoshizawa,0,0,164,,I saw the documents. They were wonderful.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:19.36,0:15:22.61,Default,Yoshizawa,0,0,164,,Good enough to be used as-is for sentencing.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:24.11,0:15:28.70,Default,Yoshizawa,0,0,164,,You wanted to be either a public prosecutor \Nor a defense lawyer, right?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:29.37,0:15:30.33,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,Yes.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:30.95,0:15:32.24,Default,Yoshizawa,0,0,164,,What do you say?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:33.62,0:15:36.25,Default,Yoshizawa,0,0,164,,Would you try aiming to become a judge?
Dialogue: 0,0:15:45.67,0:15:49.97,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,{\an8}This is the heaviest sentence Judgeman can impose.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:49.97,0:15:54.22,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,{\an8}Death Penalty accompanied by Confiscation.
Dialogue: 0,0:15:55.93,0:16:03.78,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Confiscation makes it impossible to use one's technique, \Nor in Itadori's case, his cursed energy.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:03.78,0:16:08.03,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,At the same time, Higuruma is granted \Nthe Executioner's Sword.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:08.57,0:16:16.33,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,Anyone cut by the Executioner's Sword will, \Nwithout exception, meet their death.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:17.29,0:16:23.17,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}Empathizing with another's feelings means understanding their weakness.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:23.67,0:16:27.55,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}The weakness of victims, the weakness of criminals.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:28.47,0:16:31.43,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}Day after day after day...
Dialogue: 0,0:16:32.30,0:16:34.35,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}I was so fed up.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:35.43,0:16:36.93,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}"Unsightly." {CR: So ugly.}
Dialogue: 0,0:16:36.93,0:16:41.44,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}That's what I started to think every time I tried to help someone.
Dialogue: 0,0:16:42.11,0:16:44.19,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,You're the same, Itadori!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:46.44,0:16:48.95,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,All people are weak and ugly!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:49.95,0:16:53.53,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,No matter how much you long for them \Nto have noble souls!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:56.24,0:16:58.46,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,There's nothing for you down that path!
Dialogue: 0,0:16:58.46,0:17:01.08,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,The darkness before you is just that!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:02.17,0:17:07.05,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Even if you shine a light on it, \Nyou'll just find blinding nothingness!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:13.51,0:17:14.64,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,I'm sorry.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:15.18,0:17:16.06,Default,Higuruma,0,0,164,,I won't become a judge.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:16.06,0:17:17.77,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I won't become a judge.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:22.48,0:17:23.77,Default,Yoshizawa,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:23.77,0:17:25.90,Default,Yoshizawa,0,0,0,,May I ask why not?
Dialogue: 0,0:17:27.19,0:17:30.32,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}All people are weak and ugly.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:32.66,0:17:36.54,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I'm not interested in promotions, \Nso I'm not cut out for it.
Dialogue: 0,0:17:37.54,0:17:38.62,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}However!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:39.20,0:17:40.46,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}At the time!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:40.46,0:17:42.50,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}At least up until that moment!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:43.00,0:17:49.13,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}I believed that very depravity, which no other \Ncreature possessed, was something to be cherished!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:49.55,0:17:50.38,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:51.34,0:17:52.47,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why, Itadori Yuji?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:53.18,0:17:55.26,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}Why did you admit guilt?!
Dialogue: 0,0:17:55.64,0:18:02.94,Default,Narrator,0,0,0,,The evidence that Judgeman submits \Nis shared with the sorcerer before it is opened.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:03.35,0:18:08.82,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}The evidence provided was about \Nthe demon harbored inside you called Sukuna!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:09.53,0:18:10.78,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}You didn't kill them!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:11.86,0:18:13.82,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,{\i1}So why?! Why?!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:34.09,0:18:34.89,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Hey!
Dialogue: 0,0:18:36.30,0:18:39.60,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Penal Code, Article 39, Clause 1.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:40.72,0:18:47.31,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Being deprived of either sound judgment or control \Nof one's actions qualifies as non compos mentis.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:49.19,0:18:53.57,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,In Shibuya, Sukuna had taken control of your body.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:53.57,0:18:55.49,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,How do you know about Sukuna?
Dialogue: 0,0:18:56.28,0:18:59.28,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,In other words, you lacked control of your actions.
Dialogue: 0,0:18:59.28,0:19:03.41,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,You didn't voluntarily surrender control, either.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:03.41,0:19:04.33,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,In other words,
Dialogue: 0,0:19:05.12,0:19:06.21,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,you're innocent.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:08.63,0:19:10.34,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,You've committed no crime.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:12.55,0:19:15.18,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Even so, it's still my fault.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:16.22,0:19:18.18,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Because I was too weak.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:22.14,0:19:23.48,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:24.31,0:19:28.23,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Higuruma, why did you release your technique?
Dialogue: 0,0:19:31.90,0:19:33.99,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I returned to my roots.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:35.86,0:19:42.95,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Itadori, there may still be plenty of people \Nwho are weak like you.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:44.62,0:19:46.12,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Put your clothes on.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:46.12,0:19:47.67,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Then have a seat.
Dialogue: 0,0:19:47.67,0:19:48.96,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I'll give you my 100 points.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:02.60,0:20:03.68,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Itadori.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:05.14,0:20:08.56,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Have you ever killed someone of your own volition?
Dialogue: 0,0:20:16.19,0:20:17.20,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,I have.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:23.16,0:20:24.08,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,I see.
Dialogue: 0,0:20:26.25,0:20:28.42,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,It's the worst feeling in the world. {CR: It felt absolutely awful, didn't it?}
Dialogue: 0,0:21:59.88,0:22:02.30,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Kogane, add a rule.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:03.22,0:22:07.10,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Make it possible for players \Nto transfer points to one another.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:07.93,0:22:12.73,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Of course, this should count toward \Nthe "change in points" mentioned in Rule 8.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:12.73,0:22:14.44,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,Approved.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:14.94,0:22:21.19,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,Rule 10: Players may transfer a number of points \Nof their choosing to another player.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:22.70,0:22:25.57,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Kogane, give one of my points to Itadori.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:26.12,0:22:27.70,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,As you wish.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:29.70,0:22:33.21,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,You have been granted one point \Nby Higuruma Hiromi.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:34.21,0:22:38.71,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Now neither of us will have to worry about \Nour technique being stripped for nineteen days.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:39.34,0:22:40.67,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Take care.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:41.26,0:22:42.59,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Higuruma!
Dialogue: 0,0:22:42.59,0:22:44.63,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,What are you planning to do now?
Dialogue: 0,0:22:44.63,0:22:47.22,Default,Yuji,0,0,0,,Would you like to help us? {CR: You could help us if you're willing to.}
Dialogue: 0,0:22:49.72,0:22:55.73,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,My two remaining points are from the judge and the prosecutor I killed before coming to Tokyo.
Dialogue: 0,0:22:56.98,0:23:00.44,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Once the barriers open up, I think I'll turn myself in.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:01.32,0:23:04.74,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Until then, I'll think about what I should I do.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:05.45,0:23:10.08,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Besides, if I stay with you, \NI'm likely to hate myself even more.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:11.37,0:23:14.41,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Sorry. I'm not criticizing you.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:15.92,0:23:16.92,Default,Higuruma,0,0,0,,Later.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:25.68,0:23:27.34,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\an8}A new rule will be added soon.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:27.34,0:23:30.14,Default,Kogane,0,0,0,,{\an8}...a number of points of their choosing to another player.
Dialogue: 0,0:23:30.14,0:23:31.60,Default,Reggie,0,0,0,,{\an8}If you don't fight to kill...
Dialogue: 0,0:23:31.60,0:23:32.43,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\an8}You're okay with this?!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:32.43,0:23:34.14,Default,Takaba,0,0,0,,{\an8}I don't want you as my Wi-Fi!
Dialogue: 0,0:23:34.14,0:23:36.81,Default,Fushiguro,0,0,0,,{\an8}Hand over all of your points.
